00:04:56,666 --> 00:05:02,666
Royality meets reality.

2
00:09:53,333 --> 00:09:59,333
Princess Protection Program is a family, tv movie,
comedy film directed by Allison Liddi-Brown.

3
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:56,000
When her nation is invaded, a young princess is taken
into the Princess Protection Program.

4
00:19:46,666 --> 00:19:52,666
She is relocated to Louisiana, where she stays with a covert agent and his tomboyish
daughter, and must learn how to behave like an ordinary teenager.

5
00:24:43,333 --> 00:24:49,333
Rosalinda María Montoya Fioré, played by Demi Lovato.

6
00:29:40,000 --> 00:29:46,000
Carter Mason, played by Selena Gomez.

7
00:34:36,666 --> 00:34:42,666
Ed, played by Nicholas Braun.

8
00:39:33,333 --> 00:39:39,333
Joe Mason, played by Tom Verica.

9
00:44:30,000 --> 00:44:36,000
The Director, played by Molly Hagan.

10
00:49:26,666 --> 00:49:32,666
Brooke Angels, played by Samantha Droke.

11
00:54:23,333 --> 00:54:29,333
Princess Protection Program is a 2009 American comedy film
released as a Disney Channel Original Movie.

12
00:59:20,000 --> 00:59:26,000
It is directed by Allison Liddi-Brown and stars Demi Lovato and Selena Gomez.

13
01:04:16,666 --> 01:04:22,666
The script was written by Annie DeYoung from a story
by Annie DeYoung and David Morgasen.

14
01:09:13,333 --> 01:09:19,333
The film premiered on June 26, 2009, in the United States on Disney
Channel and was released on DVD on June 30, 2009.

15
01:14:10,000 --> 01:14:16,000
The film won the 2009 Teen Choice Awards for Choice Summer Movie.

16
01:19:06,666 --> 01:19:12,666
The film explores themes of princess, high school,
friendship, island, parent child relationship.

17
01:24:03,333 --> 01:24:09,333
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
